One caveat: `dbg!()` only fires at *construction* time — when `builtin_get_time()` is called to build the tool handle during agent setup (e.g., `agent.add_tool(builtin_get_time())` in `main.rs`), which happens once at registration, not on each tool execution. If you need to trace each get_time *call*, the macro would need to go inside the async closure that computes the timestamp instead.

